{
  "name": "kaizen",
  "version": "1.39.0",
  "description": "Schema-driven workflow plugin for Claude Code. A pre-commit gatekeeper enforces iron-laws + Karpathy 4 + frontmatter / schema / coverage axes across the diff. A routine engine drives multi-stage flows — audit / build-feature / fix-bug / refactor / migrate / harden / spec-driven / onion-tdd-strict / ralph-loop — with per-stage TDD gates. A lens-driven handoff system (scaffold → verify → assess → auto-finalize → append → parent_handoff chain) keeps work continuous across sessions. Observability layers — kaizen-trace event log, dxm live mirror, systems-check heartbeat — give live + retroactive visibility. Memory: PARA-structured Second Brain (Persona / Top Beliefs / Evidence Log / Notes), kaizen-gold incidental capture, chatlog trigger-rule transcript slicer. Coding-skills library (DRY / KISS / YAGNI / SOLID / LoD / SoC / Boy-Scout / Convention) + onion-DDD + Karpathy 4. Worktree-isolated sub-agents (implementer / reviewer / debt-auditor / karpathy-reviewer / memory-analyst / skill-extractor / backlog-curator). Per-domain MCP sub-servers composed behind one FastMCP gateway. Session-bundle convention under .kaizen/superpowers/<date>-<project>-<sid8>/. Cross-platform (Linux + macOS); python3 only hard dep; self-contained.",
  "author": {
    "name": "YugeIceCone",
    "url": "https://github.com/YugeIceCone"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/YugeIceCone/kaizen-md",
  "repository": "https://github.com/YugeIceCone/kaizen-md",
  "license": "MIT",
